==Battleground==
*3 [[Doge Dark]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 13.33~16.67 seconds<sup>400f~500f</sup>.
*1 [[Ursamajor]] spawns after 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>.
*1 [[Bakoo]] spawns after 23.33 seconds<sup>700f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[White Cyclone]] spawns as the boss.
**3 [[Darkmadillo]]s spawn, delay 60~63.33 seconds<sup>1,800f~1,900f</sup>.
**2 [[Tackey]]s spawn, delay 66.67~70 seconds<sup>2,000f~2,100f</sup>.
**4 [[Li'l Bun Bun]]s spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 33.33~36.67 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,100f</sup>.
**3 [[Imperator Sael]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 80~83.33 seconds<sup>2,400f~2,500f</sup>.
**2 [[Bakoo]]s spawn after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>, delay 53.33~56.67 seconds<sup>1,600f~1,700f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Doge Dark]]s spawn after 53.33 seconds<sup>1,600f</sup>, delay 23.33~26.67 seconds<sup>700f~800f</sup>.
**2 [[Ursamajor]]s spawn after 66.67 seconds<sup>2,000f</sup>, delay 60~63.33 seconds<sup>1,800f~1,900f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This stage is more tedious than it is difficult. Using traditional meatshields and tanks will work against you later on when the Bakoos start spawning, so if a unit doesn't deal instant damage the moment they reach the frontline, it's probably best to chuck 'em. Fortunately, that leaves you with many good options to completely obliterate this stage: [[Talents|Talented]] [[Dom Cat (Special Cat)|Dark Lazer]], [[Cats in a Box (Special Cat)|Heavy Assault C.A.T.]], and [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]] completely obliterate this stage so long as you use [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]] to deal with White Cyclone. Bring along [[Biohazard (Combo)|Biohazard]] and [[Bony Bone (Combo)|Bony Bone]] to spam them even harder, since it's not like you'll be running out of cash either way. Other units like [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jelly Dumpling Cat]], [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]], and [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] are recommended.

Remember that neither of the Bakoos are boss enemies, which means pushing them behind the base—to where they aren't directly targeted by any of your cats—is a death sentence to whatever stack you've currently got built up. This is likely to happen a few times, but regrouping is trivial and it only prolongs the inevitable.

